  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 281st Trolls, the 304th Dragons, the 291st Trolls, 
the 309th Legion and the 335th Dragons in reserve.  The defenders had the 
327th Trolls, the 189th Skeletal Bowmen, the 190th Bowmen and the 301st 
Eagles in reserve.  Alain marched with his loyal troops, eyes set in grim 
determination.  Agesilao led his armies into the fray.  Negumba stood ready 
at the head of his thousands.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Babba Sissoko (#0) marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  Agesilao wielded his Holy Sword.  Alain (#33) stepped 
forward and challenged Agesilao to honorable combat.  Agesilao declined to 
enter combat.
  The forces commanded by Agesilao were disappointed by his 
faint-heartedness.  They marched on, though with shaken confidence.  Alain's 
luck was awful, for an unfounded rumor that enemy forces had destroyed all 
supplies began to sweep through his troops!  This gave Agesilao's forces a 
great advantage.  On the other hand in this chess match, Alain seemed to 
gain the tactical edge.
  Negumba was frustrated by the Eagles, who could not comprehend his 
military strategy.
  Across the entire front, the Crack 137th Skeletal Phalanx faced the Crack 
194th Skeletal Warg Riders, who were exhorted into a fanatical state by a 
retinue of clerics from the Brotherhood of Druids, who awed the soldiers 
with magical chanting.  The 126th Skeletal Dragons swooped down on the 238th 
Warg Riders and attacked them.  The 271st Dragons soared over the 34th 
Trolls and attacked them.  The 304th Dragons swooped down on the 189th 
Skeletal Bowmen and attacked without mercy.  The 335th Dragons soared over 
the 194th Skeletal Warg Riders and attacked them.  News of the perilous 
battle had spread far and wide throughout Jadegate, and even the Basilisk 
heard of it and arrived for the show, where the Basilisk fought alongside 
the 194th Skeletal Warg Riders.  The Basilisk was of some slight help in the 
contest.  On this field, the contest was a straightforward slugfest decided 
by the bravery of the soldiers themselves in melee combat.  The 137th 
Skeletal Phalanx battled the 194th Skeletal Warg Riders and were slowly bent 
back by their pressure.
  Having found a weak spot in the line of the host of Babba Sissoko (#0), a 
final determined slashing attack finished off their enemy and won the day 
for Agesilao.  The 194th Skeletal Warg Riders gave chase and scattered the 
281st Trolls in all directions.  The 238th Warg Riders overtook the enemy 
and destroyed the 137th Skeletal Phalanx.
  Although Agesilao's forces were triumphant, Alain (#33) regrouped his men 
and prepared to contest Jadegate.  Agesilao's experience improved his skill 
in Tactics.  After the battle, the trolls reformed into a horrid band of 
mercenaries.
  In late summer, Agesilao attempted an illegal move.  He was already in 
Jadegate and could make no sense of the order to move to Jadegate.  So, 
Agesilao discovered nothing in his sagely researches.

  In Jadegate, Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) campaigned against 
Agesilao.  Alain (#33) commanded the attacking armies.  The defending forces 
were led by Agesilao.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as 
shown here:

