  DEFENDING ARMY

  The defenders had the 301st Eagles in reserve.  Standing at the ready with 
his warriors was Alain.  Agesilao led a host of loyal soldiers into the 
battle.  Negumba stood determinedly at the head of his thousands.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Babba Sissoko (#0) marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  Agesilao wielded his Holy Sword.  Alain (#33) stepped 
forward and challenged Agesilao to personal combat.  Agesilao declined to 
enter personal combat.
  The forces commanded by Agesilao were disappointed by his cowardice.  They 
steadfastly marched on, though with lessened confidence.  In this battle, 
Alain had stolen a march on Agesilao and was fortunate to catch the 
defenders napping.  As the fierce battle developed, the tactical abilities 
of Agesilao and Alain seemed to be well matched and neither leader could 
achieve a tactical advantage.
  Negumba could make almost no use of the Eagles, who could not comprehend 
his commands.
  On the right wing, the Veteran 309th Legion faced the Crack 194th Skeletal 
Warg Riders.  The 126th Skeletal Dragons soared over the 34th Trolls and 
attacked without mercy.  The 335th Dragons swooped down on the 190th Bowmen 
and attacked them.  The 335th Dragons were staggered by the arrows loosed by 
those dangerous Bowmen.  The 301st Eagles swooped down on the 309th Legion 
and attacked them.  In this sector, when the commander of the 309th Legion 
spotted a weak link in the enemy line, he quickly assembled an elite force 
of picked soldiers to cut their way through it, and met with success.  The 
309th Legion battled the 194th Skeletal Warg Riders and gradually shoved 
them back.
  Out on the left outside wing, the 291st Trolls were arrayed against the 
Crack 238th Warg Riders, who were exhorted into a fanatical state by a 
retinue of druids from the Brotherhood of Druids, who awed the soldiers with 
mystical chanting.  The 271st Dragons swooped down on the 327th Trolls and 
attacked them.  The 304th Dragons soared over the 189th Skeletal Bowmen and 
attacked them.  The 304th Dragons were decimated by the arrows loosed by 
those pesky Bowmen.  The Basilisk, learning of the peril of the Druidic 
king, arrived at the battle to fight with the 238th Warg Riders.  
The Basilisk was of some slight assistance in the contest.  On this 
battleground, the commander of the 238th Warg Riders sneaked a fanatically 
religous assassin behind enemy lines.  He murdered the opposing commander in 
a rush, then committed suicide.  The 291st Trolls fought the 238th 
Warg Riders and could neither gain the upper hand nor could the enemy make 
any headway.
  The battle ended in victory for the soldiers of Alain as they broke 
through at a critical moment.  The 126th Skeletal Dragons chased after the 
enemy and demolished the 194th Skeletal Warg Riders.  The 271st Dragons 
pursued the enemy and destroyed the 327th Trolls.  The 335th Dragons gave 
chase and were beaten off by the 238th Warg Riders in a hard-fought 
rearguard action.  The 304th Dragons overtook the enemy and slew the 189th 
Skeletal Bowmen almost to a man.
  Jadegate was overrun by the forces of Alain.  The battle affected the 
quality of our forces:  the 34th Trolls was badly shaken during the battle 
and we must now rate it as a Green unit.  Agesilao fell back to Black Forest 
with his forces.  Negumba withdrew to Black Forest, beaten but not 
discouraged.  After the battle, the trolls regenerated into a disgruntled 
band of mercenaries.

  In Mare Frigidis, Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) brought to bay 
Agesilao.  Hope (#94) commanded the invading armies.  The defending forces 
were commanded by the provincial garrison commander.  The armies were drawn 
up into lines of battle as shown here:

