  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 36th Skeletal Garrison in reserve.  Hope commanded a 
host of loyal soldiers.  No generals were present to lead the forces of 
Agesilao.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Babba Sissoko (#0) marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  Hope (#94) was unlucky, for she had been unable to find a 
suitable encampment to rest her troops the previous day, thus her men were 
in poor shape.  On the other hand in this slugging match, Hope appeared to 
have the tactical edge.
  Agesilao's soldiers swore to fight desperately for their fatherland.
  Across the whole front, the Veteran 134th Skeletal Warg Riders were 
arrayed against the 344th Skeletal Garrison.  The 340th Skeletal Warg Riders 
and the 125th Skeletal Phalanx outflanked the undermanned enemy and charged 
in with full strength.  The 134th Skeletal Warg Riders fought with the 344th 
Skeletal Garrison and determinedly plowed into their opponents.
  Hope's great horde overwhelmed the army of Agesilao and took the field, 
dispersing their enemies.  The 134th Skeletal Warg Riders annihilated the 
344th Skeletal Garrison.
  Hope's well-planned campaign effected the conquest of Mare Frigidis.  The 
acting commander retreated to Black Forest.
  With the coming of the fall season Agesilao's attempted cast of the Plague 
spell didn't work.
  A diplomatic furor erupted between the Realms of Agesilao (whose alliances 
are too incompatible) and Uga-Buga Makumb (#1), degrading their diplomatic 
relations 1 level(s)!
  The fall cooled into a frigid early winter.  Agesilao marched his command 
into Katmai (#108).


  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to Agesilao invaded the province 
of Katmai, a Forest area ruled by Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0).  
Agesilao commanded the invading armies.  The defenders were commanded by 
Alain (#33).  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

