  DEFENDING ARMY

  Agesilao commanded a host of loyal soldiers.  Standing tall with his 
warriors was Alain.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Babba Sissoko (#0) marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  Agesilao drew out his Holy Sword.  Alain (#33) strode 
forward and challenged Agesilao to personal combat.  Agesilao refused to 
enter combat.
  The forces commanded by Agesilao were disappointed by his 
faint-heartedness.  They marched on, though with shaken confidence.  
Agesilao was not at all fortunate this day, because the sun shone directly 
against his men's eyes, giving Alain's men a small edge.  Also, his tactical 
maneuvers failed to succeed as expected, and his men fought with a slight 
tactical disadvantage.

  Out on the left wing, the Crack 238th Warg Riders faced the Green 189th 
Skeletal Bowmen.  The 126th Skeletal Dragons swooped down on the 238th 
Warg Riders and attacked them.  The 238th Warg Riders fought with the 189th 
Skeletal Bowmen and were trampled over like oversized pumpkins.
  In the interior lines, the 190th Bowmen were exhorted into a fanatical 
fury by a retinue of druids from the Brotherhood of Druids, who awed the 
soldiers with magical chanting.  They were arrayed against the Crack 194th 
Skeletal Warg Riders.  Helping the 190th Bowmen in the battle was the Treant,
coming to the defense of its friend, the Druidic ruler.  The Treant was of 
some slight assistance in the battle.  The 271st Dragons swooped down on the 
190th Bowmen and attacked without mercy.  The 271st Dragons were decimated 
by the bolts loosed by the pesky Bowmen.  The 190th Bowmen battled with the 
194th Skeletal Warg Riders and were knocked out of the fight by the enemy's 
fanatical charge.
  On the right wing, the Green 34th Trolls were arrayed against the Crack 
309th Legion.  The 304th Dragons soared over the 34th Trolls and attacked 
them.  The 34th Trolls battled the 309th Legion and were cut down like 
sheep.
  The host of Alain finally broke the army of Agesilao's fighting spirit 
with one last, great push.  The 194th Skeletal Warg Riders annihilated the 
190th Bowmen.  The 309th Legion destroyed the 34th Trolls.  The 126th 
Skeletal Dragons pursued the enemy and scattered the 238th Warg Riders in 
all directions.
  The defenders defeated Agesilao's forces and drove them out of Katmai.  
His forces completely dispersed, Agesilao escaped frightened and alone to 
Black Forest.
  Thus endeth the adventures of Agesilao for this year.


  Agesilao treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Agesilao treated with his 
ally Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3).  Agesilao treated with his ally Hokuto (#4).
Agesilao treated with his ally Prometeo (#5).  Agesilao treated with his 
ally II Kahn (#6).  Agesilao treated with his ally Giovanna d'Arco (#7).  
Agesilao treated with his ally Circe (#8).

  Here is the financial report for Agesilao's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 31 gold in revenue.  3 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  5 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Agesilao was left 
with 54 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Tancred
To: Agesilao

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I moved into the Arrak Sea.
  With the coming of the early summer season, I tried a Skeletal Army spell, 
but botched it.  My efforts raised my skill in Necromancy.
  Midsummer's day passed and a hot late summer arrived.  I rode into the 
Ixitxachitl Sea.  To the south lay an icy wasteland which extends as far as 
the eye can see.
  During fall, I travelled to the Mariner Sea.  To the south icy wastes 
stretch to join the horizon.  Looking to the west, one can see a Plain area, 
which is known as Tanglewood (#1309).  It is populated by Dwarves and 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango rules there.  Their Dwarven fighters fight 
in the style of Axemen and Light Cavalry.
  Adonis (#69) encountered me.  Casting a Hand Of Death spell, Adonis 
directed glowing, interlacing strands of magic and began making squeezing 
motions with his hands.  I stuck my tail between my legs and fled from 
Adonis as fast as my legs could carry me!
  The fall season cooled into early winter.  I rode into Tanglewood.  To the 
south is a mass of glaciers which has no end.  West of here is Redwood 
(#1209), a poor Forest area owned by Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango, where 
Trolls dwell.  If need be, they can muster a host of Trolls to defend their 
territory.  To the northwest there lies a Mountain province known as Piratum 
(#1208), a rich land of Orcs where Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango reigns.  
Their Orcish fighters prefer to array themselves as Phalanx and Warg Riders.

  Thy humble servant,   Tancred


From: Negumba
To: Agesilao

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season I set out to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  The plague struck the 125th Skeletal Phalanx in Mare Frigidis 
and destroyed them.  The plague struck the 134th Skeletal Warg Riders in 
Mare Frigidis and destroyed them.  The plague struck the 136th Skeletal 
Warg Riders in Mare Frigidis and destroyed them.  The plague struck the 
340th Skeletal Warg Riders in Mare Frigidis and destroyed them.  I rode my 
flying armies over to Black Forest.
  During early summer, I, responsible for the defense of Black Forest, 
learned of an enemy move on Jadegate.  I rode my flying armies over to 
Jadegate.
  With the coming of the late summer season I tried to practice my Tactics, 
but the task seemed beyond my natural ability.
  With the coming of the fall season Negumba's Plague spell backfired and I 
was left covered with psycho-kinetic goo.
  The fall cooled into a frigid early winter.  I prepared my armies to 
defend Black Forest and the surrounding provinces.

  Thy humble servant,   Negumba


From: Tonto, Squire to Stonebrick
To: Agesilao

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Stonebrick was magically killed by a dark Necromantic spell!  
And so it came to pass that Stonebrick met his unseemly end.

  Thy humble servant,   Tonto, Squire to Stonebrick


